[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   TEP-9 step 101 -- Interstellar-object non-gravitational channel
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   The three catalogued interstellar objects are the only population
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   besides comets that physically transits the outer boundary sector on
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   measurable trajectories.  Step 099 scored their inbound asymptotes
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   geometrically; this step tests the *dynamical* channel: the fitted
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   non-gravitational (NG) acceleration parameters in the JPL SBDB orbit
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   solutions against the boundary-sector geometry each trajectory
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   threaded.
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   The discriminating observable is not the presence of NG -- every
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   outgassing comet carries fitted NG terms -- but an *unexplained* NG:
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   a fitted acceleration with no detected volatile driver.  Literature
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   anchors (transcribed published values, ``iso_literature.json``)
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   record that 1I/'Oumuamua's NG is unexplained by any detected mass
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   loss (~25 kg/s required, ~3 orders of magnitude above observed
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   limits) while 2I/Borisov's and 3I/ATLAS's are accounted for by
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   measured gas and dust production.
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   Geometry scored per object
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   * arrival and departure velocity-asymptote directions (computed from
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   the SBDB osculating hyperbolic elements: position directions at
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   nu = -nu_inf and nu = +nu_inf), and the periapsis direction that
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   sets the sky sector of the inner observed arc;
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   * separations against the pre-declared axis (49,-17) and antiaxis
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   (229,+17), classified as lobe (<60 deg, the measured cap radius),
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   edge band (60-75 deg, the measured transition width of step 073),
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   or field;
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   * a bipolar double-lobe transit flag -- arrival through one 60-deg
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   lobe and departure through the other -- the geometry under which
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   the two boundary crossings compound rather than cancel in the
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   bipolar slip field (steps 052, 089).
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   Tests
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   T1 sector concordance: does unexplained-NG incidence coincide with
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   the bipolar double-lobe transit?  Exchangeability weight reported
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   (n = 3; descriptive, not a detection claim).
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   T2 magnitude: implied fractional effective-attraction offset
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   f(r) = |a_ng(r)| / g_sun(r) evaluated under each solution's own
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   Marsden-Sekanina g(r) law at r = q, 1 au, 2 au; compared with the
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   comet-channel lapse contrast (step 100, implied dA/A).
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   T3 vector morphology: |A2/A1| and |A3/A1| transverse fractions and
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   perihelion-time offset DT -- a directed-gradient signature is
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   radial-dominant while rotational-jet outgassing loads power into
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   the transverse component and asymmetric activity requires DT.
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   T4 inner-arc sector: the periapsis-direction sector each inner
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   observed arc sampled vs the measured cos-2theta sign structure
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   (step 089: positive dtau at both axis poles, negative in the
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   60-120 deg mid-band).  Borisov's fully volatile-explained NG
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   bounds any *universal interior* lapse-gradient term on a
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   mid-band inner arc at its fitted amplitude -- extending the
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   wall-over-field verdict of step 068 into the inner system.
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   T5 prospective registration: pre-declared NG-class predictions for
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   future ISO arrivals by transit geometry.
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   T6 classification stability: single-member reclassification audit --
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   the T1 concordance is load-bearing on the volatile classes, so
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   each object's reclassification consequence is computed and the
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   monitored channel (SBDB solution evolution, the 3I mass-
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   accounting caveat) registered; publicly discussed 3I oddities
[2026-09-20 12:19:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 101]   are triaged as non-lapse channels.
